a resource consent is permission to  undertake an activity or to construct a  building that does not comply with the  district plan rules it requires you to  consider the effects of your projects on  the environment the community and your  neighbors  you'll also need a results content for  subdividing the land or resource consent  is different from a building consent  which covers how something is  constructed to comply with the Building  Act to apply for resource consent you  will need to compile the relevant  documentation for a subdivision you will  need a surveyor to produce survey plans  otherwise the plans would usually be  drawn by an architect or draftsperson  one of the most important things you'll  need to provide is an assessment of the  environmental effects an AE e you can  ask a consultant planner surveyor or  architect to prepare this for you if the  proposal is small in scale you may wish  to prepare this yourself council  planners can give you guidance on this  an AE e describes the effects of your  proposed activity on the surrounding  environment and on your neighbors the  complexity of your assessment will  depend on the scale of your proposal  let's look at some things that would  normally trigger a resource consent  Andrea wants to extend her garden area  and needs to do some earthworks at the  back of her property and her assessment  of the environmental effects she details  how they go into landscape and build a  retaining wall to protect the bank from  slips and reduce the visual effects John  wants to construct a second-story on his  house his assessment of effects would  need to consider if the addition will  have an unfair impact on his neighbors  such as shading and loss of privacy  Susie wants to open a childcare center  she will need to identify and assess any  potential effects such as noise in  traffic she may put up acoustic fencing  and provide a traffic management plan to  mitigate adverse effects of noise and  traffic if you think that your activity  may have an effect on your neighbor then  you should seek their approval council  will assist your proposal and then visit  your property they will assess the  effects on your neighbors and the  surrounding area if you have provided  your neighbors written approval with  your application then the planner will  not need to consider if they are  affected as long as all the relevant  information is supplied council will  provide you with a decision after 20  working days if your resource consent is  granted make sure you read and  understand your conditions the  posle must be undertaken as shown on  your plans so make sure you get it right  first time as it may be difficult to  change later  [Music]
 

